prompt:
Long-running servers of a combat game slowly climb in memory over several hours until they lag. Server code (simplified):
```lua
local sessions = {}
Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(function(player)
    sessions[player] = { kills = 0, history = {} }
    player.CharacterAdded:Connect(function(char)
        RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function()
            updateAura(char)
        end)
    end)
end)
```
Nothing else cleans up. Identify the leaks and give the fixes.

responses.R4:
Leaks: (1) A new Heartbeat connection is created on every CharacterAdded and never disconnected; after each respawn the old ones keep running on dead characters (holding references to destroyed models, so they are never GC'd), and the per-frame cost grows with every death. (2) sessions[player] is never cleared, so every player who ever joined (Player object + history) stays in memory; history is also unbounded. (3) Connections to player.CharacterAdded are fine once the Player is destroyed, but the strong table reference keeps it alive. Fixes:

local auraConns = {}
Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(function(player)
  sessions[player] = { kills = 0, history = {} }
  player.CharacterAdded:Connect(function(char)
    if auraConns[player] then auraConns[player]:Disconnect() end
    auraConns[player] = RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function() updateAura(char) end)
    char.Destroying:Once(function() if auraConns[player] then auraConns[player]:Disconnect(); auraConns[player] = nil end end)
  end)
end)
Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(function(player)
  if auraConns[player] then auraConns[player]:Disconnect(); auraConns[player] = nil end
  sessions[player] = nil
end)

Cap history (ring buffer / trim old entries). Better still: one global Heartbeat loop iterating active characters. Set workspace.PlayerCharacterDestroyBehavior = Enabled so old characters are destroyed.

responses.R5:
Leaks: (1) sessions[player] is never removed. Every player who has joined stays in the table (the history keeps growing too), and the Player object is held, so it is never garbage-collected. (2) Every respawn adds a new Heartbeat connection. None of them are disconnected, so they pile up, keep running on dead characters and keep the old char models referenced. (3) The CharacterAdded connection lives with the player and is released when the player is destroyed, but the Heartbeat ones aren't. Fixes:
```lua
local conns = {}
Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(function(player)
    sessions[player] = { kills = 0, history = {} }
    player.CharacterAdded:Connect(function(char)
        if conns[player] then conns[player]:Disconnect() end
        conns[player] = RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function() updateAura(char) end)
    end)
end)
Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(function(player)
    if conns[player] then conns[player]:Disconnect(); conns[player] = nil end
    sessions[player] = nil
end)
```
Also disconnect when the Humanoid dies or on char.Destroying, and cap the history (ring buffer). Better still, run one Heartbeat loop over all active characters instead of one per player. Watch the server's memory with Developer Console > Memory and LuaHeap.
